                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Rating: 8.4/10\n\nEarth 2160 is a science-fiction real-time strategy game that combines large-scale battles, resource management, base building, and a futuristic setting. Players can choose between several different factions, each with their own units, technologies, and playstyles, and must manage their economy while building an army capable of defeating opposing forces. The game offers a fairly traditional RTS structure, but its futuristic setting and wide range of units give it a distinct identity.\n\nOne of the strongest aspects of Earth 2160 is the amount of variety available during gameplay. The different factions provide noticeably different approaches to combat, while the large selection of units and technologies gives players plenty of options when developing their strategies. Building a strong economy and adapting to the enemy are important parts of the experience, and large battles can become quite entertaining once players have access to more advanced technology. The campaign also helps introduce the game's mechanics while providing a substantial amount of content for players interested in the setting.\n\nHowever, the game can feel somewhat dated, particularly when it comes to its interface, controls, and presentation. Some mechanics are not as polished or intuitive as those found in more modern strategy games, and the learning curve can occasionally make certain aspects feel unnecessarily complicated. Despite these issues, Earth 2160 remains an interesting RTS for players who enjoy older strategy games and futuristic warfare. Its faction variety, extensive technology systems, and large-scale battles make it a solid choice for fans of classic science-fiction real-time strategy games.",
